<EXPERIMENT_PACKAGE><EXPERIMENT alias="GSM4094349" accession="SRX6894908"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRX6894908</PRIMARY_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>GSM4094349: Patient_18_normal; Homo sapiens; RNA-Seq</TITLE><STUDY_REF accession="SRP193095"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP193095</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioProject">PRJNA533799</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS></STUDY_REF><DESIGN><DESIGN_DESCRIPTION/><SAMPLE_DESCRIPTOR accession="SRS5427795"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS5427795</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM4094349</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SAMPLE_DESCRIPTOR><LIBRARY_DESCRIPTOR><LIBRARY_STRATEGY>RNA-Seq</LIBRARY_STRATEGY><LIBRARY_SOURCE>TRANSCRIPTOMIC</LIBRARY_SOURCE><LIBRARY_SELECTION>cDNA</LIBRARY_SELECTION><LIBRARY_LAYOUT><PAIRED/></LIBRARY_LAYOUT><LIBRARY_CONSTRUCTION_PROTOCOL>Total RNA was extracted from ESCC tissues using TRIzol reagent (Invitrogen) for construction of RNA-seq libraries. The sequencing library was prepared from 1 ug of total RNA using Illumina TruSeq Stranded Total RNA Library Prep Kit with Ribo-Zero Human/Mouse/Rat (RS-122-2203).</LIBRARY_CONSTRUCTION_PROTOCOL></LIBRARY_DESCRIPTOR></DESIGN><PLATFORM><ILLUMINA><INSTRUMENT_MODEL>Illumina HiSeq 2000</INSTRUMENT_MODEL></ILLUMINA></PLATFORM><EXPERIMENT_LINKS><EXPERIMENT_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>gds</DB><ID>304094349</ID><LABEL>GSM4094349</LABEL></XREF_LINK></EXPERIMENT_LINK></EXPERIMENT_LINKS><EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTES><EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>GEO Accession</TAG><VALUE>GSM4094349</VALUE></EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTE></EXPERIMENT_ATTRIBUTES></EXPERIMENT><SUBMISSION alias="GEO: GSE130078" broker_name="GEO" center_name="GEO" submission_comment="submission brokered by GEO" lab_name="" accession="SRA877387"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRA877387</PRIMARY_ID><SUBMITTER_ID namespace="GEO">GEO: GSE130078</SUBMITTER_ID></IDENTIFIERS></SUBMISSION><Organization type="center"><Name abbr="GEO">NCBI</Name><Contact email="geo-group@ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"><Name><First>Geo</First><Last>Curators</Last></Name></Contact></Organization><STUDY center_name="GEO" alias="GSE130078" accession="SRP193095"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRP193095</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioProject" label="primary">PRJNA533799</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSE130078</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_TITLE>A Novel LincRNA HERES Epigenetically Regulates Wnt Signaling Pathway via Interaction with EZH2 in Esophageal Squamous Cell Carcinoma</STUDY_TITLE><STUDY_TYPE existing_study_type="Transcriptome Analysis"/><STUDY_ABSTRACT>Esophageal squamous cell carcinoma (ESCC), a major type of primary esophageal cancer in developing countries, displays a very poor clinical outcome in five-year survival rate. Although long non-coding RNAs (lncRNAs) exert critical roles in cancer development, the promising therapeutic targets of ESCC-expressed lncRNAs have not been comprehensively examined and their cancer-driving roles remain largely unknown at the mechanistic level. In this study, we aimed to identify ESCC-driving lncRNAs in the transcriptome level and exploit a therapeutic target with understanidng their modes of action. Overall design: High-throughput RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) was performed with rRNA-depleted, total RNAs prepared from paired cancerous and non-cancerous tissues of 23 Korean ESCC patients, and the RNA-seq data were profiled to identify ESCC-driving lncRNAs.</STUDY_ABSTRACT><CENTER_PROJECT_NAME>GSE130078</CENTER_PROJECT_NAME></DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>pubmed</DB><ID>31732666</ID></XREF_LINK></STUDY_LINK></STUDY_LINKS></STUDY><SAMPLE alias="GSM4094349" accession="SRS5427795"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS5427795</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN12828238</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM4094349</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>Patient_18_normal</TITLE><SAMPLE_NAME><TAXON_ID>9606</TAXON_ID><SCIENTIFIC_NAME>Homo sapiens</SCIENTIFIC_NAME></SAMPLE_NAME><SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>bioproject</DB><ID>533799</ID><LABEL>PRJNA53